# Byte-exactness is a research requirement here, not a style preference.
#
# This repository freezes research artifacts by SHA-256 and asks independent
# reviewers to verify those digests. Git's automatic end-of-line conversion made
# that impossible: a file checked out on Windows differed byte for byte from the
# same file on Linux, so a declared hash was reproducible on one platform only.
# 843 of 1348 files under data/ were affected. See issue #26.
#
# `-text` disables all conversion, so a checkout reproduces the stored blob
# exactly on every platform. It is chosen over `text=auto eol=lf` because
# normalising would rewrite the stored bytes of existing artifacts and break the
# declared hashes that are currently correct.
* -text
